WEBVTT

00:00:11.380 --> 00:00:14.380
KABUKICHO ICHIBANGAI

00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:19.720
<i>It was in a blind spot</i>
<i>in a forest of neon signs,</i>

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:23.480
<i>the shadow of buildings that</i>
<i>nobody would usually pay attention to.</i>

00:00:24.690 --> 00:00:28.230
<i>But somehow, at that time,</i>
<i>he glanced in the direction.</i>

00:00:29.270 --> 00:00:31.820
<i>In a small open space</i>
<i>behind the buildings,</i>

00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:35.200
<i>a mortal combat was about to begin.</i>

00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:37.870
<i>Are they going to have a fight?</i>

00:00:38.530 --> 00:00:42.790
<i>Fighting against such a big man,</i>
<i>he'll get himself killed.</i>

00:00:44.370 --> 00:00:45.710
You're insane.

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:47.920
Had you observed me more carefully,

00:00:48.040 --> 00:00:53.130
you'd have realized I'm not a decent man
and much stronger than you are.

00:00:53.880 --> 00:00:56.550
But you picked a fight with me.

00:00:56.890 --> 00:00:58.850
I'm sure you're not sane.

00:00:59.050 --> 00:01:00.470
<i>He is absolutely right.</i>

00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:02.100
Huh?

00:01:05.310 --> 00:01:07.350
You're stronger than me?

00:01:08.230 --> 00:01:11.230
Don't talk nonsense.
Just show me how strong you are.

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:12.610
Big shit.

00:01:13.240 --> 00:01:14.990
<i>What? Seriously?!</i>

00:01:15.610 --> 00:01:17.030
<i>Now he's a dead man.</i>

00:01:18.320 --> 00:01:19.830
I'm totally right.

00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:22.040
You're insane.

00:01:23.370 --> 00:01:27.420
<i>The big man looked</i>
<i>just like the guardian God Nio.</i>

00:01:28.290 --> 00:01:29.170
<i>In fact,</i>

00:01:30.290 --> 00:01:33.840
<i>the guardian God was sitting on his back.</i>

00:01:34.340 --> 00:01:38.140
<i>What's that body?!</i>
<i>He's like the </i>Terminator.

00:01:38.260 --> 00:01:40.850
<i>There is no way</i>
<i>he can beat that monster down.</i>

00:01:43.600 --> 00:01:46.180
<i>He's used to fighting as I thought.</i>

00:01:47.190 --> 00:01:50.770
<i>Too fast!</i>
<i>How can a huge guy like him move so fast?</i>

00:01:54.610 --> 00:01:55.650
<i>That's not it.</i>

00:01:55.990 --> 00:01:56.860
<i>His advantage is...</i>

00:01:59.450 --> 00:02:02.620
<i>He crushed the concrete wall</i>
<i>with just one kick!</i>

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:08.000
I knew it. Those are iron-plated boots.

00:02:08.620 --> 00:02:11.170
I really don't want to get those kicks.

00:02:12.420 --> 00:02:14.170
<i>There's no way he can win.</i>

00:02:14.670 --> 00:02:18.550
<i>A slender handsome guy easily beats</i>
<i>a man of gigantic build?</i>

00:02:19.010 --> 00:02:22.010
<i>That always happens in fiction.</i>
<i>But...</i>

00:02:22.390 --> 00:02:25.890
<i>Fantasy like that has no chance</i>
<i>to exist in the real world.</i>

00:02:26.680 --> 00:02:27.680
Hey...

00:02:28.100 --> 00:02:30.060
Stop running around.

00:02:30.520 --> 00:02:32.610
This is the fight you picked.

00:02:32.860 --> 00:02:36.030
-Now it's your turn--
-Okay. Here I come!

00:02:41.620 --> 00:02:43.240
Son of a bitch!

00:02:49.330 --> 00:02:50.420
He's injured.

00:02:50.830 --> 00:02:52.330
Now you understand...

00:02:53.540 --> 00:02:55.630
Which one of us is the challenger, huh?

00:03:01.130 --> 00:03:02.220
<i>Well, well...</i>

00:03:04.100 --> 00:03:05.890
<i>I'll get the power of his punch...</i>

00:03:07.350 --> 00:03:09.230
<i>fully turned back on him.</i>

00:03:11.270 --> 00:03:12.350
Wow.

00:03:12.770 --> 00:03:14.690
Your arm is completely dislocated.

00:03:14.900 --> 00:03:16.150
I can still--

00:03:17.940 --> 00:03:19.030
Still what?

00:03:19.280 --> 00:03:21.360
You're wrong.

00:03:23.070 --> 00:03:26.580
You've been finished already.

00:03:36.590 --> 00:03:37.460
<i>He...</i>

00:03:39.210 --> 00:03:40.970
<i>He won!</i>

00:03:41.760 --> 00:03:43.300
It's done.

00:03:49.220 --> 00:03:50.850
Y-- Your name...

00:03:52.230 --> 00:03:53.770
May I have your name?

00:03:55.480 --> 00:03:57.610
<i>The question just came out of his mouth.</i>

00:03:57.900 --> 00:04:01.110
<i>Though the man was as young as his sons,</i>

00:04:01.320 --> 00:04:06.370
<i>the highest respect for a stronger male</i>
<i>clearly arose in his heart.</i>

00:04:08.030 --> 00:04:09.410
Ohma Tokita.

00:04:09.950 --> 00:04:13.540
Mr. Ohma Tokita...

00:04:14.040 --> 00:04:15.170
And...

00:04:16.130 --> 00:04:17.290
your name is?

00:04:17.710 --> 00:04:19.550
Oh, you're...

00:04:19.920 --> 00:04:22.220
asking my name?

00:04:24.510 --> 00:04:25.430
I'm...

00:04:28.560 --> 00:04:31.140
I am Kazuo Yamashita, sir!

00:04:32.180 --> 00:04:34.810
You're Kazuo Yamashita?

00:04:36.100 --> 00:04:37.150
Okay.

00:04:37.770 --> 00:04:38.770
Then...

00:04:40.610 --> 00:04:42.320
you want to fight, too?

00:04:42.820 --> 00:04:43.700
What?!

00:04:45.030 --> 00:04:46.740
<i>What pressure!</i>

00:04:47.240 --> 00:04:48.990
<i>This can't be a joke.</i>

00:04:49.450 --> 00:04:50.740
<i>He's serious.</i>

00:04:52.120 --> 00:04:53.330
<i>I'll be killed.</i>

00:04:54.580 --> 00:04:55.920
<i>I can't breathe...</i>

00:04:57.460 --> 00:04:58.540
No.

00:05:00.090 --> 00:05:01.670
You don't?

00:05:02.760 --> 00:05:04.420
That's disappointing.

00:05:19.110 --> 00:05:21.480
<i>Kazuo Yamashita, 56 years old.</i>

00:05:22.150 --> 00:05:24.190
<i>He is a serious, married man</i>
<i>with two sons.</i>

00:05:24.530 --> 00:05:28.490
<i>The man who in the prime of his life never</i>
<i>drunk, gambled or paid for sex,</i>

00:05:29.070 --> 00:05:33.540
<i>slept with a woman that night</i>
<i>for the first time in 15 years.</i>

00:05:34.120 --> 00:05:35.910
<i>What urged him was...</i>

00:05:36.670 --> 00:05:38.540
<i>the instinct of self-preservation.</i>

00:05:39.290 --> 00:05:43.880
<i>Exposed to an extremely murderous</i>
<i>atmosphere that he'd never experienced,</i>

00:05:44.300 --> 00:05:47.430
<i>his instinct immediately sensed</i>
<i>the great danger of life.</i>

00:05:48.340 --> 00:05:51.390
<i>Feeling cornered, he chose instinctively</i>
<i>to preserve the species</i>

00:05:51.470 --> 00:05:52.890
<i>as soon as possible.</i>

00:05:53.270 --> 00:05:56.520
<i>Therefore, he ended up</i>
<i>being engaged in reproductive activity.</i>

00:05:57.350 --> 00:06:01.650
<i>However, he never knew</i>
<i>what caused him to do it.</i>

00:06:11.950 --> 00:06:16.870
KENGAN

00:06:20.960 --> 00:06:21.920
NOGI PUBLICATIONS

00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:23.460
<i>Yamashita.</i>

00:06:24.050 --> 00:06:26.760
You're below quota this month, too.

00:06:26.840 --> 00:06:29.010
I sincerely apologize for it.

00:06:29.550 --> 00:06:31.760
I'll make it next month for sure.

00:06:31.850 --> 00:06:33.560
KAZUO YAMASHITA
NOGI PUBLICATIONS, NOGI GROUP

00:06:33.720 --> 00:06:36.770
"Next month"?
You say the same thing every month.

00:06:36.850 --> 00:06:38.600
HIROSHI MATSUI
NOGI PUBLICATIONS, NOGI GROUP

00:06:38.690 --> 00:06:40.650
To be honest,
your words are not very convincing.

00:06:41.230 --> 00:06:44.270
<i>Chief is picking on Mr. Yamashita again.</i>

00:06:44.400 --> 00:06:48.150
<i>Dumping all the bothersome tasks</i>
<i>on to Mr. Yamashita, Chief does nothing.</i>

00:06:48.570 --> 00:06:50.780
-Are you listening to me?
-Yes, of course!

00:06:50.910 --> 00:06:52.410
I have no excuse.

00:06:52.620 --> 00:06:56.660
<i>Darn it! He's just a kid</i>
<i>who got his job through nepotism.</i>

00:06:57.540 --> 00:07:00.960
<i>If I were as strong as that man,</i>

00:07:01.080 --> 00:07:04.880
<i>I would treat this jerk like this!</i>

00:07:05.550 --> 00:07:06.840
<i>Am I stupid?</i>

00:07:07.010 --> 00:07:10.340
<i>I'm bowing because I can't do that.</i>

00:07:10.720 --> 00:07:12.050
Sorry to disturb you.

00:07:12.470 --> 00:07:13.930
President!

00:07:14.010 --> 00:07:16.220
If you needed me,
you could have called me to your office.

00:07:16.310 --> 00:07:17.970
FUTOSHI HOSOME
NOGI PUBLICATIONS, NOGI GROUP

00:07:18.100 --> 00:07:19.560
It's not you whom I want to see.

00:07:20.440 --> 00:07:21.520
Yamashita.

00:07:21.850 --> 00:07:25.150
Someone special wants to have
a private word with you.

00:07:25.860 --> 00:07:28.110
Visit him immediately
to ask what he needs.

00:07:28.360 --> 00:07:29.240
Huh?

00:07:29.400 --> 00:07:30.280
Um...

00:07:30.450 --> 00:07:32.780
Is it really him?

00:07:33.280 --> 00:07:34.620
Oh, man...

00:07:35.700 --> 00:07:39.330
What kind of mess did you make?

00:07:39.700 --> 00:07:40.580
Sorry?

00:07:43.790 --> 00:07:47.000
NOGI GROUP HEADQUARTERS

00:07:52.680 --> 00:07:54.470
Thank you for taking your time.

00:07:54.550 --> 00:07:56.050
HIDEKI NOGI,
CHAIRMAN OF NOGI GROUP

00:07:56.140 --> 00:07:58.100
Sorry to bother you while you're busy.

00:07:58.310 --> 00:08:01.270
No problem at all, sir!

00:08:02.600 --> 00:08:05.650
<i>A mere cog of one of the subsidiaries</i>
<i>is summoned</i>

00:08:05.860 --> 00:08:07.860
<i>by the chairman of the group companies?</i>

00:08:08.530 --> 00:08:10.690
<i>What on earth did I do?</i>

00:08:12.030 --> 00:08:13.240
Conflicts.

00:08:14.990 --> 00:08:18.160
What do you think is the best way...

00:08:18.830 --> 00:08:20.700
to solve a conflict?

00:08:21.080 --> 00:08:24.250
To solve... a conflict?

00:08:24.670 --> 00:08:25.670
Right.

00:08:26.080 --> 00:08:29.880
The word "solve" is simple,
but we have millions of ways to do it,

00:08:30.460 --> 00:08:33.260
such as by mediating, negotiating,
and persuading.

00:08:34.010 --> 00:08:35.590
The most effective one is...

00:08:36.590 --> 00:08:37.890
by using violence.

00:08:38.640 --> 00:08:41.180
U-- Using violence?

00:08:41.930 --> 00:08:46.350
You bear down on your enemy with violence
which overwhelms them.

00:08:46.980 --> 00:08:49.440
<i>That doesn't solve a conflict itself.</i>

00:08:52.940 --> 00:08:54.450
You're right.

00:08:55.910 --> 00:09:00.580
Of course, violence could be
effective as a safety system,

00:09:01.040 --> 00:09:04.750
but that's only
when the violence is under control.

00:09:05.370 --> 00:09:09.130
We can gain nothing
from disorganized violence.

00:09:09.540 --> 00:09:12.130
That would only result in
unstoppable tyrannies.

00:09:15.050 --> 00:09:20.260
<i>In 1715, although the Edo period was</i>
<i>such a peaceful age,</i>

00:09:20.600 --> 00:09:26.690
<i>the bloody conflicts among merchants</i>
<i>existed at all times.</i>

00:09:27.650 --> 00:09:34.490
<i>What they desired was the highest and</i>
<i>exclusive privilege as a merchant:</i>

00:09:36.780 --> 00:09:38.870
<i>to be a vendor to the Imperial Court.</i>

00:09:40.450 --> 00:09:46.120
<i>They used every possible way, such as</i>
<i>threat, conspiracy or assassination...</i>

00:09:47.120 --> 00:09:51.710
<i>to kick their competitors out</i>
<i>of their business field.</i>

00:09:52.590 --> 00:09:55.170
<i>The chain of violence</i>
<i>had expanded so widely...</i>

00:09:56.090 --> 00:10:01.760
<i>that even the merchants themselves</i>
<i>had no way of controlling it.</i>

00:10:02.430 --> 00:10:05.930
<i>The world was about to descend</i>
<i>into pandemonium.</i>

00:10:09.770 --> 00:10:12.150
<i>The times needed some rules...</i>

00:10:12.770 --> 00:10:15.490
<i>to control the fighting.</i>

00:10:16.610 --> 00:10:19.610
<i>Ietsugu Tokugawa, the 7th shogun,</i>

00:10:19.820 --> 00:10:23.410
<i>summoned the merchants</i>
<i>at the center of the troubles,</i>

00:10:23.660 --> 00:10:25.870
<i>and he gave them an order.</i>

00:10:27.790 --> 00:10:32.710
<i>If you want to settle a fight,</i>
<i>you should have a clean showdown.</i>

00:10:33.800 --> 00:10:37.760
<i>It was such a simple and straight</i>
<i>suggestion from a child.</i>

00:10:38.380 --> 00:10:40.340
<i>However, nobody among them</i>

00:10:40.550 --> 00:10:45.850
<i>could come up with this simple answer.</i>

00:10:47.230 --> 00:10:48.980
<i>As you wish.</i>

00:10:50.230 --> 00:10:52.520
<i>Order was brought to violence.</i>

00:10:54.150 --> 00:10:58.820
<i>The merchants organized an association</i>
<i>through which they held a match</i>

00:10:59.150 --> 00:11:02.870
<i>when there was a conflict of interests</i>
<i>among them.</i>

00:11:04.120 --> 00:11:06.870
<i>The rule was quite simple:</i>

00:11:07.200 --> 00:11:09.910
<i>a one-on-one battle, unarmed.</i>

00:11:10.920 --> 00:11:13.670
<i>The highly skilled fighters</i>
<i>hired by both sides</i>

00:11:13.880 --> 00:11:16.090
<i>fought each other on behalf</i>
<i>of the merchants</i>

00:11:16.250 --> 00:11:18.010
<i>until the winner was announced.</i>

00:11:19.380 --> 00:11:24.010
<i>In due course, violence was</i>
<i>developed into a martial art.</i>

00:11:25.760 --> 00:11:29.770
One of the association members was
my ancestor.

00:11:30.270 --> 00:11:36.360
Nogi Group owes him
its current prosperity.

00:11:37.440 --> 00:11:38.570
<i>So what?</i>

00:11:39.400 --> 00:11:40.860
<i>What's the point of this story?</i>

00:11:41.240 --> 00:11:44.910
Do you understand
why I'm telling this story to you?

00:11:46.370 --> 00:11:49.450
The story is not just an old tale.

00:11:49.870 --> 00:11:55.590
It's a traditional fighting method
still practiced by merchants today.

00:11:56.630 --> 00:11:58.630
Oh, no... Are you joking?

00:11:59.210 --> 00:12:01.050
It's too hard for me to believe it.

00:12:02.220 --> 00:12:03.760
<i>He seems so serious.</i>

00:12:04.140 --> 00:12:06.720
<i>Was he telling the truth?</i>

00:12:07.310 --> 00:12:12.390
Even after Japan has been modernized,
the merchants have handed down

00:12:12.560 --> 00:12:17.730
this duel system for generations
to solve their conflicts.

00:12:18.520 --> 00:12:21.610
<i>Setting your hopes on the fighter's fists</i>
<i>is the meaning of...</i>

00:12:23.110 --> 00:12:24.780
<i>"kengan match."</i>

00:12:26.070 --> 00:12:28.950
<i>What's a kengan match?!</i>

00:12:29.330 --> 00:12:32.660
In fact, we're going to have a match
in a few days

00:12:32.790 --> 00:12:35.540
with some other companies
over a specific right.

00:12:35.880 --> 00:12:39.210
But we have a little problem.

00:12:39.800 --> 00:12:46.260
<i>The man we originally hired is unable</i>
<i>to join the match for some reasons.</i>

00:12:46.590 --> 00:12:50.850
<i>We need to look</i>
<i>for another fighter, quickly.</i>

00:12:52.480 --> 00:12:53.640
Oh, no...

00:12:54.350 --> 00:12:56.150
Are you telling me to fight?

00:12:58.110 --> 00:13:00.020
That's not a bad idea.

00:13:00.400 --> 00:13:03.530
Unfortunately, that won't be necessary.

00:13:03.950 --> 00:13:06.910
As soon as we started recruiting
a new fighter,

00:13:07.120 --> 00:13:09.620
a man came to us and offered himself.

00:13:10.370 --> 00:13:13.830
We decided to leave this match up to him.

00:13:18.670 --> 00:13:20.250
Here he comes.

00:13:23.800 --> 00:13:28.930
<i>Unbelievable!</i>
<i>Is he going to be the substitute fighter?</i>

00:13:29.470 --> 00:13:32.430
Let me introduce our fighter to you.

00:13:32.520 --> 00:13:33.380
He is Ohma Tokita.

00:13:33.480 --> 00:13:35.240
OHMA TOKITA
AFFILIATED FIGHTER OF NOGI GROUP

00:13:35.350 --> 00:13:37.270
Good to see you again, Kazuo Yamashita.

00:13:37.380 --> 00:13:39.650
It's my pleasure to see you again, too.

00:13:39.900 --> 00:13:43.400
<i>What a miraculous coincidence!</i>

00:13:43.990 --> 00:13:47.240
Oh, you two know each other?

00:13:47.780 --> 00:13:49.950
That would be even more convenient.

00:13:50.450 --> 00:13:52.080
Kazuo Yamashita.

00:13:52.620 --> 00:13:56.460
I'll assign you to take care of him.

00:13:57.920 --> 00:13:59.040
Tokita.

00:13:59.460 --> 00:14:03.760
If you need anything,
don't hesitate to ask him.

00:14:04.380 --> 00:14:05.470
All right.

00:14:06.220 --> 00:14:08.890
Why don't you have a meeting
to discuss the future plan?

00:14:09.090 --> 00:14:11.600
Details will be announced later.

00:14:16.480 --> 00:14:17.890
Was it really a good idea...

00:14:18.350 --> 00:14:20.270
to trust that man?

00:14:22.570 --> 00:14:25.780
The one who beat Komada is probably...

00:14:26.240 --> 00:14:28.070
I believe that's him.

00:14:28.450 --> 00:14:30.240
That's why I hired him.

00:14:30.870 --> 00:14:36.080
How many people in the world
do you think can take Komada down?

00:14:36.660 --> 00:14:38.040
Ohma Tokita.

00:14:38.410 --> 00:14:40.670
We were very lucky to find him.

00:14:40.880 --> 00:14:42.040
What about the other one?

00:14:42.500 --> 00:14:43.400
Kazuo Yamashita.

00:14:43.500 --> 00:14:45.930
KAEDE AKIYAMA, SECRETARY TO
THE OFFICE OF CHAIRMAN OF NOGI GROUP

00:14:46.040 --> 00:14:47.920
He's just an employee of
one of our subsidiaries.

00:14:48.000 --> 00:14:51.150
Why did you tell him
what a kengan match is, sir?

00:14:51.930 --> 00:14:56.180
We have plenty of other people
better at taking care of the fighter.

00:14:56.600 --> 00:14:58.060
Well...

00:14:58.680 --> 00:14:59.810
No special reason.

00:15:00.520 --> 00:15:01.560
Excuse me?

00:15:03.150 --> 00:15:04.820
Don't get so annoyed.

00:15:05.150 --> 00:15:09.400
I assigned him not only for support,
but also to keep an eye on him for safety.

00:15:09.900 --> 00:15:11.240
That's all.

00:15:12.030 --> 00:15:14.700
<i>It doesn't explain why you chose him, sir.</i>

00:15:15.700 --> 00:15:18.120
<i>Is it because you don't want</i>
<i>to tell me about it?</i>

00:15:18.790 --> 00:15:20.250
<i>Ohma Tokita.</i>

00:15:20.540 --> 00:15:22.330
<i>I'll find out...</i>

00:15:23.420 --> 00:15:26.000
<i>what kind of man you are.</i>

00:15:29.260 --> 00:15:31.800
Please... please wait!

00:15:33.760 --> 00:15:36.060
What's wrong, Kazuo Yamashita?

00:15:36.390 --> 00:15:37.890
<i>Why does he call me by my full name?</i>

00:15:38.470 --> 00:15:43.350
Mr. Tokita.
You should decline his offer.

00:15:43.560 --> 00:15:46.150
Fighting a duel is a crime.

00:15:46.440 --> 00:15:48.280
How could Chairman Nogi think such--

00:15:48.400 --> 00:15:50.610
Hey, first of all...

00:15:51.780 --> 00:15:52.950
let's go eat.

00:15:55.450 --> 00:15:56.330
Yes.

00:15:57.450 --> 00:15:59.000
<i>"Let's go eat."</i>

00:15:59.450 --> 00:16:03.620
<i>Spoken by him,</i>
<i>such a simple phrase like this</i>

00:16:04.250 --> 00:16:07.380
<i>sounds so violent</i>
<i>that it's impossible for you to resist.</i>

00:16:08.920 --> 00:16:10.880
<i>In Ohma Tokita's dictionary,</i>

00:16:11.010 --> 00:16:15.140
<i>the word "reconsidering"</i>
<i>doesn't even exist in the first place.</i>

00:16:15.220 --> 00:16:17.890
SEVEN DAYS LEFT UNTIL THE KENGAN MATCH!

00:16:26.360 --> 00:16:28.980
<i>Good morning, everyone.</i>

00:16:29.150 --> 00:16:32.030
<i>I am Kazuo Yamashita.</i>

00:16:32.320 --> 00:16:35.280
<i>I've been working for Nogi Publications</i>
<i>for 34 years.</i>

00:16:35.490 --> 00:16:38.830
<i>At age 56, I'm still</i>
<i>in my most productive years.</i>

00:16:39.490 --> 00:16:41.200
<i>"Having a fulfilling private life,</i>

00:16:42.000 --> 00:16:43.960
<i>I'm satisfied every day."</i>

00:16:44.750 --> 00:16:45.960
<i>That's not my case.</i>

00:16:47.210 --> 00:16:48.380
Your breakfast...

00:16:49.460 --> 00:16:50.670
is here.

00:16:57.800 --> 00:17:00.640
<i>That's my older son, Kenzo.</i>

00:17:01.140 --> 00:17:05.140
<i>If I'm right,</i>
<i>he'll turn 25 years old this year.</i>

00:17:05.600 --> 00:17:08.940
<i>Since junior high school, he's been</i>
<i>shutting himself away from society</i>

00:17:09.360 --> 00:17:10.480
<i>up until now.</i>

00:17:10.860 --> 00:17:15.240
<i>The last time I saw his face was</i>
<i>two years-- No, three years ago, maybe.</i>

00:17:15.950 --> 00:17:21.740
<i>My younger son has got rebellious since</i>
<i>he dropped out of high school last year.</i>

00:17:22.250 --> 00:17:24.870
<i>He's hanging out with bad friends.</i>

00:17:25.160 --> 00:17:30.170
<i>He only comes back home</i>
<i>to steal money from my wallet.</i>

00:17:32.800 --> 00:17:36.260
<i>My wife ran away from us ten years ago.</i>

00:17:37.300 --> 00:17:41.060
<i>I still don't know why she dumped me.</i>

00:17:42.310 --> 00:17:48.940
<i>I only have this house</i>
<i>on a small patch of land left</i>

00:17:49.400 --> 00:17:53.110
<i>with the mortgage to be paid</i>
<i>for 15 years more.</i>

00:17:53.610 --> 00:17:56.450
<i>This is just where I'm going to die.</i>

00:18:10.960 --> 00:18:13.210
Is this here?

00:18:14.010 --> 00:18:16.800
I think I followed the map correctly.

00:18:17.430 --> 00:18:21.640
So this is really... Ohma's house?

00:18:22.260 --> 00:18:25.390
It's an abandoned building, isn't it?

00:18:29.480 --> 00:18:31.690
Of course, it's broken.

00:18:35.400 --> 00:18:38.200
Excuse me.

00:18:39.110 --> 00:18:41.200
Ohma?

00:18:44.240 --> 00:18:46.540
<i>Have I come to the wrong place?</i>

00:18:49.290 --> 00:18:51.130
Ohma.

00:18:51.880 --> 00:18:53.540
Are you home?

00:18:55.460 --> 00:18:58.510
<i>The floor has completely rotted away.</i>

00:19:00.930 --> 00:19:01.800
<i>What was that?</i>

00:19:03.140 --> 00:19:04.430
<i>What's going on?</i>

00:19:12.650 --> 00:19:15.360
I'm coming in.

00:19:15.730 --> 00:19:17.780
Ohma.

00:19:31.830 --> 00:19:34.000
Blood!

00:19:34.130 --> 00:19:36.380
Stay away, murderer!

00:19:36.500 --> 00:19:37.840
What are you doing?

00:19:38.340 --> 00:19:39.590
Oh?

00:19:40.680 --> 00:19:41.880
Ohma.

00:19:42.340 --> 00:19:46.600
What are you doing?
You are badly injured.

00:19:46.720 --> 00:19:49.520
I'll call the ambulance right now.

00:19:50.180 --> 00:19:51.480
Ah, this?

00:19:51.940 --> 00:19:53.400
It's not mine.

00:19:53.730 --> 00:19:55.060
I was removing blood.

00:19:55.310 --> 00:19:56.860
What? Removing blood?

00:19:57.190 --> 00:19:59.070
Yeah, from that.

00:19:59.530 --> 00:20:00.400
"That"?

00:20:03.410 --> 00:20:05.490
You're such a noisy guy.

00:20:09.160 --> 00:20:10.710
Sure you don't want any?

00:20:10.790 --> 00:20:12.540
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:20:13.000 --> 00:20:14.750
I'm not hungry.

00:20:15.250 --> 00:20:17.000
That's a shame.

00:20:19.050 --> 00:20:22.590
<i>Just look at that extraordinary body!</i>

00:20:23.090 --> 00:20:26.640
<i>Aesthetically speaking,</i>
<i>it's top-ranking anatomy.</i>

00:20:27.050 --> 00:20:30.310
<i>It's like an ancient Greek statue.</i>

00:20:31.230 --> 00:20:34.150
<i>Hey, what am I thinking?</i>

00:20:34.310 --> 00:20:36.980
<i>I don't have that kind</i>
<i>of preference at all.</i>

00:20:37.820 --> 00:20:39.400
By the way, Ohma.

00:20:39.730 --> 00:20:41.740
How on earth did you get that boar?

00:20:41.820 --> 00:20:43.110
I killed it.

00:20:43.900 --> 00:20:46.740
Killed? Why did you do a thing like that?

00:20:47.580 --> 00:20:48.660
"Why"?

00:20:49.030 --> 00:20:50.750
What else do you normally eat?

00:20:51.450 --> 00:20:53.250
You kill something to live.

00:20:54.750 --> 00:20:56.330
<i>That's correct.</i>

00:20:57.460 --> 00:20:59.630
<i>No matter how much civilization advances,</i>

00:21:00.090 --> 00:21:02.050
<i>our nature will not change.</i>

00:21:02.510 --> 00:21:05.090
<i>Now we enjoy the end product only.</i>

00:21:05.510 --> 00:21:08.470
<i>Paying no attention to the procedure</i>
<i>which surely exists.</i>

00:21:08.640 --> 00:21:12.850
<i>We kill and eat to live,</i>
<i>just like he does.</i>

00:21:13.310 --> 00:21:17.270
<i>What a straight and simple answer!</i>

00:21:17.770 --> 00:21:20.900
<i>But simple words can directly</i>
<i>convey the true story.</i>

00:21:21.230 --> 00:21:23.490
<i>I see the reality in it.</i>

00:21:24.530 --> 00:21:28.120
<i>Ohma's words are definitely true.</i>

00:21:29.990 --> 00:21:30.910
Hey.

00:21:31.790 --> 00:21:33.080
Kazuo Yamashita.

00:21:33.870 --> 00:21:35.830
You brought your buddies today?

00:21:36.120 --> 00:21:37.000
Pardon?

00:21:42.090 --> 00:21:43.460
What?!

00:21:51.100 --> 00:21:52.520
What a mess.

00:21:53.390 --> 00:21:55.680
How can you live in such a dump?

00:21:56.890 --> 00:21:58.770
Who are those people?

00:21:59.060 --> 00:22:00.610
What do you want?

00:22:00.980 --> 00:22:02.570
Soliciting? No thanks.

00:22:02.940 --> 00:22:04.280
I'll take care of this.

00:22:04.820 --> 00:22:05.950
Don't interfere.

00:22:07.320 --> 00:22:08.200
All right.

00:22:09.780 --> 00:22:11.660
I see it... a fighter’s spirit.

00:22:12.080 --> 00:22:14.450
Wait. Hold on a second.

00:22:15.000 --> 00:22:17.710
Is it possible that he is Ivan Karaev?

00:22:17.830 --> 00:22:19.080
You know him?

00:22:19.330 --> 00:22:23.670
He's a Russian kickboxer
who's been standing out recently.

00:22:24.000 --> 00:22:25.970
What is he doing here?

00:22:26.510 --> 00:22:27.720
Nothing personal.

00:22:28.510 --> 00:22:29.680
This is just business.

00:22:30.850 --> 00:22:33.560
You're going to have to stay in bed
for a while.

00:24:05.980 --> 00:24:07.070
PREVIEW

00:24:07.150 --> 00:24:09.650
<i>Extraordinary techniques</i>
<i>and gifts of heaven.</i>

00:24:09.780 --> 00:24:12.280
<i>A strong enemy beyond human rules</i>

00:24:12.360 --> 00:24:14.570
<i>stands like a wall before Ashura.</i>

00:24:14.820 --> 00:24:17.490
<i>The crisis level is immeasurable.</i>

00:24:17.830 --> 00:24:19.240
<i>Next episode:</i>
<i>"Super Human"</i>

00:24:19.370 --> 00:24:20.910
Subtitle translation by Hinako Someno
